  "id": "COMPOUND:637 - PROTEIN:349",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Dyphylline and cAMP-specific 3',5'-cyclic phosphodiesterase 4B, as both Dyphylline and the intermediate compound 3,5-Dimethyl-1-(3-Nitrophenyl)-1h-Pyrazole-4-Carboxylic Acid Ethyl Ester are linked to this enzyme. Dyphylline is directly associated with Fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase 1, which in turn is a target of both 3,5-Dimethyl-1-(3-Nitrophenyl)-1h-Pyrazole-4-Carboxylic Acid Ethyl Ester and Rolipram. Rolipram itself is also a target of cAMP-specific 3',5'-cyclic phosphodiesterase 4B, indicating a pathway through which these compounds may influence the enzyme's activity. The high scores across all three paths suggest a consistent and robust relationship, likely mediated through the intermediate targets. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Dyphylline and the enzyme, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
